[{:db/id 17592186110778 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2b8aa940-8e5f-5fd6-a1b0-b18405dff657"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2b8aa940-8e5f-5fd6-a1b0-b18405dff657" :question/id #uuid "2b8aa940-8e5f-5fd6-a1b0-b18405dff657" :question/math-academy-id "q-53011" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6ada3cc0fcd02f363da922e9537d3f832cd616886da84f63e65085bd271aa3e0.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the rectangle above?\n\nI. $∠BCD$ is not a right angle.\n\nII. $\\overset{―}{AD}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are parallel.\n\nIII. $BC=CD.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. A rectangle is a parallelogram where all angles are right. Therefore, $∠BCD$ is a right angle.\n\n- Statement II is true. The opposite sides of a rectangle are parallel, so $\\overset{―}{AD}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are parallel.\n\n- Statement III is false. Opposite sides of a rectangle are congruent, however, $BC$ and $CD$ are adjacent and we see that $BC\\ne CD.$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b909ad7e-6288-5330-b18b-d4332e6e69e4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b909ad7e-6288-5330-b18b-d4332e6e69e4" :answer-field/id #uuid "b909ad7e-6288-5330-b18b-d4332e6e69e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-92cbbb20-640e-5d85-8433-6e6a415bd113" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fd559331-35f7-58ab-877a-14827b89cf19" "answer-fe52eb10-47ee-5fd1-bfca-3c219b4d2d9c" "answer-a7cac4dc-2679-5603-a932-b379a986241e" "answer-92cbbb20-640e-5d85-8433-6e6a415bd113" "answer-81dd0b82-3bdc-58b9-aace-0499be563ebd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fd559331-35f7-58ab-877a-14827b89cf19" :answer/id #uuid "fd559331-35f7-58ab-877a-14827b89cf19" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe52eb10-47ee-5fd1-bfca-3c219b4d2d9c" :answer/id #uuid "fe52eb10-47ee-5fd1-bfca-3c219b4d2d9c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a7cac4dc-2679-5603-a932-b379a986241e" :answer/id #uuid "a7cac4dc-2679-5603-a932-b379a986241e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92cbbb20-640e-5d85-8433-6e6a415bd113" :answer/id #uuid "92cbbb20-640e-5d85-8433-6e6a415bd113" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81dd0b82-3bdc-58b9-aace-0499be563ebd" :answer/id #uuid "81dd0b82-3bdc-58b9-aace-0499be563ebd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110777 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-33255947-d8b8-558c-b5b9-74099a601ba7" "question-6ffd60c0-4297-5e49-a178-11a94ccb47c6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-33255947-d8b8-558c-b5b9-74099a601ba7" :question/id #uuid "33255947-d8b8-558c-b5b9-74099a601ba7" :question/math-academy-id "q-53031" :question/problem "![](images/fe/fe3724e266b68939b97f07fd7f428173ff0693b0d309d085187e44a45ba466ac.png)\n\nWhich of the figures above is a kite?" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.\n\n![](images/1d/1dbe4c3e8ea97c0ac077c37143802366c5817d86965ab1dbc5abf54cd01d27c3.png)\n\nRemember that a kite is a quadrilateral with two pairs of congruent sides that are adjacent to each other.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each shape in turn.\n\n- The shape $P$ is a trapezoid. It doesn't have two pairs of congruent sides that are adjacent to each other, therefore, it is not a kite.\n\n- The shape $Q$ is a rectangle. Since it doesn't have two pairs of congruent sides that are adjacent to each other, it is not a kite.\n\n- The shape $R$ is a rhombus. Therefore, it has two pairs of congruent sides that are adjacent to each other, so it is a kite.\n\n- The shape $S$ is a parallelogram. Any two adjacent sides are not congruent with each other, therefore, it is not a kite.\n\nTherefore, only shape $R$ is a kite." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8aa685bd-830c-5c31-bbf0-5ff6dfa7d380"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8aa685bd-830c-5c31-bbf0-5ff6dfa7d380" :answer-field/id #uuid "8aa685bd-830c-5c31-bbf0-5ff6dfa7d380" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-533ff24d-0dd5-597d-81d4-ef34db14a4d2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c1bb7450-f341-5f68-89ad-4d37a81dadfb" "answer-95a90f98-8016-522b-90ea-a421361fd65d" "answer-533ff24d-0dd5-597d-81d4-ef34db14a4d2" "answer-57efc2a7-dd61-536c-bba1-56239c4d994b" "answer-bd7493e8-0792-51c0-8f9c-1ab66d7e9c0c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c1bb7450-f341-5f68-89ad-4d37a81dadfb" :answer/id #uuid "c1bb7450-f341-5f68-89ad-4d37a81dadfb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P,$ $R$ and $S$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95a90f98-8016-522b-90ea-a421361fd65d" :answer/id #uuid "95a90f98-8016-522b-90ea-a421361fd65d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-533ff24d-0dd5-597d-81d4-ef34db14a4d2" :answer/id #uuid "533ff24d-0dd5-597d-81d4-ef34db14a4d2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-57efc2a7-dd61-536c-bba1-56239c4d994b" :answer/id #uuid "57efc2a7-dd61-536c-bba1-56239c4d994b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$S$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd7493e8-0792-51c0-8f9c-1ab66d7e9c0c" :answer/id #uuid "bd7493e8-0792-51c0-8f9c-1ab66d7e9c0c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6ffd60c0-4297-5e49-a178-11a94ccb47c6" :question/id #uuid "6ffd60c0-4297-5e49-a178-11a94ccb47c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-53038" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b15000ac7f2de0770140ba289a8f5224433bfb6570d985ab184eacba016c97c4.png)\n\nWhich of the figures above is a rectangle?" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.\n\n![](images/1d/1dbe4c3e8ea97c0ac077c37143802366c5817d86965ab1dbc5abf54cd01d27c3.png)\n\nRemember that a rectangle is a quadrilateral where all angles are right with two pairs of parallel sides.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each shape in turn.\n\n- The shape $P$ is an isosceles trapezoid. It has no right angles, therefore, it is not a rectangle.\n\n- The shape $Q$ is a square. Therefore, all its angles are right, so it is a rectangle.\n\n- The shape $R$ is a rectangle since all its angles are right.\n\n- The shape $S$ is a kite. Since there are no pairs of parallel sides, it is not a rectangle.\n\nTherefore, shapes $Q$ and $R$ are rectangles. The shapes $P$ and $S$ are not rectangles." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e718d457-5460-5935-99e9-b9a4df1c718d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e718d457-5460-5935-99e9-b9a4df1c718d" :answer-field/id #uuid "e718d457-5460-5935-99e9-b9a4df1c718d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ccadcf93-d50b-58d0-9015-33e93c374069" :answer-field/choices ["answer-20a142cb-5a03-56b5-9608-5de7dc8a4e1d" "answer-ccadcf93-d50b-58d0-9015-33e93c374069" "answer-d45dc88e-eeff-51ce-b206-d2acb0e76ad6" "answer-5158fa1a-17a4-51ee-8896-bddf8a29d1e8" "answer-7adc4555-752a-5e57-bcb0-83e8ec2f53d1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20a142cb-5a03-56b5-9608-5de7dc8a4e1d" :answer/id #uuid "20a142cb-5a03-56b5-9608-5de7dc8a4e1d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccadcf93-d50b-58d0-9015-33e93c374069" :answer/id #uuid "ccadcf93-d50b-58d0-9015-33e93c374069" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d45dc88e-eeff-51ce-b206-d2acb0e76ad6" :answer/id #uuid "d45dc88e-eeff-51ce-b206-d2acb0e76ad6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$, $R$ and $S$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5158fa1a-17a4-51ee-8896-bddf8a29d1e8" :answer/id #uuid "5158fa1a-17a4-51ee-8896-bddf8a29d1e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7adc4555-752a-5e57-bcb0-83e8ec2f53d1" :answer/id #uuid "7adc4555-752a-5e57-bcb0-83e8ec2f53d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-2630917f-aced-5106-9904-8233756f6371" :activity/id #uuid "2630917f-aced-5106-9904-8233756f6371" :activity/title "Classifying Quadrilaterals" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049068 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-e319bf65-c10b-5a7b-a690-7eba1bdc7f18" "step-eef9ecda-4b2e-53de-8198-669f60557288" "step-adc711d8-746b-5e53-b6c3-e0b7e18d4113"] :activity/first-step "step-e319bf65-c10b-5a7b-a690-7eba1bdc7f18" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-e319bf65-c10b-5a7b-a690-7eba1bdc7f18" :step/id #uuid "e319bf65-c10b-5a7b-a690-7eba1bdc7f18" :step/content "question-2b8aa940-8e5f-5fd6-a1b0-b18405dff657" :step/next "step-eef9ecda-4b2e-53de-8198-669f60557288" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-eef9ecda-4b2e-53de-8198-669f60557288" :step/id #uuid "eef9ecda-4b2e-53de-8198-669f60557288" :step/content "question-33255947-d8b8-558c-b5b9-74099a601ba7" :step/next "step-adc711d8-746b-5e53-b6c3-e0b7e18d4113" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-adc711d8-746b-5e53-b6c3-e0b7e18d4113" :step/id #uuid "adc711d8-746b-5e53-b6c3-e0b7e18d4113" :step/content "question-6ffd60c0-4297-5e49-a178-11a94ccb47c6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166736 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-17398103-0726-57d3-aad8-24938a444c94"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167151 :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(11)$ given below, compute $P(X<10).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ | $10$ | $11$ | $12$ | $13$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.1432\\,$ | $\\,0.2320\\,$ | $\\,0.3405\\,$ | $\\,0.4599\\,$ | $\\,0.5793\\,$ | $\\,0.6887\\,$ | $\\,0.7813\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<10) & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,9\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 9) \\\\  & =F(9) \\\\  & =0.3405.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163956 :answer-field/correct 17592186163961 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166737 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d8455b7b-7c5b-5bab-ac5b-3afa70d37c46"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186167152 :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(6)$ given below, compute $P(2<X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0620\\,$ | $\\,0.1512\\,$ | $\\,0.2851\\,$ | $\\,0.4457\\,$ | $\\,0.6063\\,$ | $\\,0.7440\\,$ | $\\,0.8472\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(5) & =P(X\\le 5) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X\\in \\{3,4,5\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(2<X\\le 5) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(2<X\\le 5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X\\le 5) & =F(5)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.4457-0.0620 \\\\  & =0.3837.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186163962 :answer-field/correct 17592186163967 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-d8455b7b-7c5b-5bab-ac5b-3afa70d37c46" :question/id #uuid "d8455b7b-7c5b-5bab-ac5b-3afa70d37c46" :question/math-academy-id "q-224966" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(8)$ given below, compute $P(4<X\\le 6).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0138\\,$ | $\\,0.0424\\,$ | $\\,0.0996\\,$ | $\\,0.1912\\,$ | $\\,0.3134\\,$ | $\\,0.4530\\,$ | $\\,0.5925\\,$ |\n\n$P(4<X\\le 6)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(6) & =P(X\\le 6) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,…,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3,4\\})+P(X\\in \\{5,6\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 4)+P(4<X\\le 6) \\\\  & =F(4)+P(4<X\\le 6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(4<X\\le 6) & =F(6)-F(4) \\\\  & =0.3134-0.0996 \\\\  & =0.2138.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-170b17fe-2985-5e8e-adef-2c16c5db1659"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-170b17fe-2985-5e8e-adef-2c16c5db1659" :answer-field/id #uuid "170b17fe-2985-5e8e-adef-2c16c5db1659" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1dc688eb-61f5-52d8-bf95-9b58a000fa0e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1dc688eb-61f5-52d8-bf95-9b58a000fa0e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dc688eb-61f5-52d8-bf95-9b58a000fa0e" :answer/id #uuid "1dc688eb-61f5-52d8-bf95-9b58a000fa0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.2138" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-17398103-0726-57d3-aad8-24938a444c94" :question/id #uuid "17398103-0726-57d3-aad8-24938a444c94" :question/math-academy-id "q-224994" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(7)$ given below, find the value of $P(X\\le 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0009\\,$ | $\\,0.0073\\,$ | $\\,0.0296\\,$ | $\\,0.0818\\,$ | $\\,0.1730\\,$ | $\\,0.3007\\,$ | $\\,0.4497\\,$ |\n\n$P(X\\le 5)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 5) & =F(5) \\\\  & =0.3007.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b2ff7417-ca9e-560f-ae90-1cd48c8905de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b2ff7417-ca9e-560f-ae90-1cd48c8905de" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2ff7417-ca9e-560f-ae90-1cd48c8905de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-9fae328c-89f2-563a-a5a4-668ae4227a93" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9fae328c-89f2-563a-a5a4-668ae4227a93"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9fae328c-89f2-563a-a5a4-668ae4227a93" :answer/id #uuid "9fae328c-89f2-563a-a5a4-668ae4227a93" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3007" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186166738 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-27647abc-efb3-57c0-813d-ce357897815d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-27647abc-efb3-57c0-813d-ce357897815d" :question/id #uuid "27647abc-efb3-57c0-813d-ce357897815d" :question/math-academy-id "q-225086" :question/problem "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(9)$ given below, compute $P(X\\ge 8).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0212\\,$ | $\\,0.0550\\,$ | $\\,0.1157\\,$ | $\\,0.2068\\,$ | $\\,0.3239\\,$ | $\\,0.4557\\,$ | $\\,0.5874\\,$ |\n\n$P(X\\ge 8)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 8)=P(X>7).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 8) & =P(X>7) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 7) \\\\  & =1-F(7) \\\\  & =1-0.3239 \\\\  & =0.6761.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f6a0816c-2f64-5562-b7f4-1cfc7a5ea04a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f6a0816c-2f64-5562-b7f4-1cfc7a5ea04a" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6a0816c-2f64-5562-b7f4-1cfc7a5ea04a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-888157ba-107f-5a5c-97c9-d6b5387c773f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-888157ba-107f-5a5c-97c9-d6b5387c773f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-888157ba-107f-5a5c-97c9-d6b5387c773f" :answer/id #uuid "888157ba-107f-5a5c-97c9-d6b5387c773f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6761" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-fada443e-8034-5b67-8dc8-1b9292803e76" :activity/id #uuid "fada443e-8034-5b67-8dc8-1b9292803e76" :activity/title "The CDF of the Poisson Distribution" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049899 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-c2457db8-1ad7-55ba-80b6-98094e23625b" "step-296bb2e2-9a40-524a-8c