} {:db/id "step-5a4d1833-4de6-5b7f-a0f8-71dae918ac36" :step/id #uuid "5a4d1833-4de6-5b7f-a0f8-71dae918ac36" :step/content 17592186363479 :step/next "step-20784d43-677f-59ca-8373-aae6aa0ba306" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-20784d43-677f-59ca-8373-aae6aa0ba306" :step/id #uuid "20784d43-677f-59ca-8373-aae6aa0ba306" :step/content 17592186493914 :step/next "step-6afc1d96-44ae-5e1f-9336-bfac0ae66fd7" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-6afc1d96-44ae-5e1f-9336-bfac0ae66fd7" :step/id #uuid "6afc1d96-44ae-5e1f-9336-bfac0ae66fd7" :step/content 17592186363493 :step/next "step-4be30a34-e97f-5f10-b37d-f500fef61f28" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4be30a34-e97f-5f10-b37d-f500fef61f28" :step/id #uuid "4be30a34-e97f-5f10-b37d-f500fef61f28" :step/content 17592186532620 :step/next "step-2dd20d76-a35b-5263-a3ea-2332a52e4990" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2dd20d76-a35b-5263-a3ea-2332a52e4990" :step/id #uuid "2dd20d76-a35b-5263-a3ea-2332a52e4990" :step/content 17592186172385 :db/ensure [:step/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186177909 :answer-field/choices 17592186177910] [:db/retract 17592186177909 :answer-field/choices 17592186177911] [:db/retract 17592186177909 :answer-field/choices 17592186177912] [:db/retract 17592186177909 :answer-field/choices 17592186177914] {:db/id 17592186180040 :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)=(x+y)\\,i+(y-x)\\,j$ across the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$ \n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & =x+y=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t), \\\\ Q(x,y) & =y-x=3(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t))\\cdot (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-(3(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t))\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({cos}^{2}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =9t{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =9(2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =18\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177909 :answer-field/correct "answer-1d03d1d4-83e8-5434-ba88-654e772f6034" :answer-field/choices ["answer-94ef6336-a885-5e0f-9339-fb9e597d51dc" "answer-2bedcbb9-3a20-535c-92e0-bda037bb0531" "answer-1d03d1d4-83e8-5434-ba88-654e772f6034" "answer-c61c8d76-f473-524c-b92c-3be06cc40c20"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-94ef6336-a885-5e0f-9339-fb9e597d51dc" :answer/id #uuid "94ef6336-a885-5e0f-9339-fb9e597d51dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bedcbb9-3a20-535c-92e0-bda037bb0531" :answer/id #uuid "2bedcbb9-3a20-535c-92e0-bda037bb0531" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d03d1d4-83e8-5434-ba88-654e772f6034" :answer/id #uuid "1d03d1d4-83e8-5434-ba88-654e772f6034" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c61c8d76-f473-524c-b92c-3be06cc40c20" :answer/id #uuid "c61c8d76-f473-524c-b92c-3be06cc40c20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204011 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fe1475b2-e88a-5639-9c34-aefc361e0ff5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204445 :question/problem "Consider two sets of $25$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{25},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{25}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{x}_{i}=250, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{y}_{i}=265, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{25}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=3\\,625.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${S}_{xy}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the statistic ${S}_{xy}$ be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & =3\\,625-\\frac{1}{25}(250)(265) \\\\  & =3\\,625-2\\,650 \\\\  & =975.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186202606 :answer-field/correct "answer-2e208d22-eade-509b-b9cd-26f67b90dab5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2e208d22-eade-509b-b9cd-26f67b90dab5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e208d22-eade-509b-b9cd-26f67b90dab5" :answer/id #uuid "2e208d22-eade-509b-b9cd-26f67b90dab5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "975" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fe1475b2-e88a-5639-9c34-aefc361e0ff5" :question/id #uuid "fe1475b2-e88a-5639-9c34-aefc361e0ff5" :question/math-academy-id "q-251794" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $14$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{14},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{14}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{14}{x}_{i}=157, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{14}{y}_{i}=182, \\\\  & {\\sum }_{i=1}^{14}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}=2\\,227.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, ${S}_{xy}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the statistic ${S}_{xy}$ be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}{y}_{i}-\\frac{1}{n}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{y}_{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given statistics in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & =2\\,227-\\frac{1}{14}(157)(182) \\\\  & =2\\,227-2\\,041 \\\\  & =186.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-73feca10-d97d-5b59-8725-6847129335cf"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-73feca10-d97d-5b59-8725-6847129335cf" :answer-field/id #uuid "73feca10-d97d-5b59-8725-6847129335cf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-386c5691-b5b0-5909-a9d6-cd57208e04fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-386c5691-b5b0-5909-a9d6-cd57208e04fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-386c5691-b5b0-5909-a9d6-cd57208e04fd" :answer/id #uuid "386c5691-b5b0-5909-a9d6-cd57208e04fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "186" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204010 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-72d27b98-5424-5f73-97fc-8f2eaa4b8548"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186204009 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f9b76f6d-a314-5376-893f-3c9706a4c31e"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f9b76f6d-a314-5376-893f-3c9706a4c31e" :question/id #uuid "f9b76f6d-a314-5376-893f-3c9706a4c31e" :question/math-academy-id "q-251858" :question/problem "Consider two sets of $39$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{39},$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{39}.$ You are given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx}=663,\\,{S}_{yy}=1\\,092,\\,{S}_{xy}=975.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, $Cov(x,y)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ their covariance can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{n},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${S}_{xy}$ is the sum of products of the deviations of ${x}_{i}$ and ${y}_{i}$ from their means.\n\nWe are given that ${S}_{xy}=975.$ Substituting the given statistic in the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Cov(x,y) & =\\frac{975}{39} \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9daa41b5-a3c9-591b-8bf6-1fa87f56a85e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9daa41b5-a3c9-591b-8bf6-1fa87f56a85e" :answer-field/id #uuid "9daa41b5-a3c9-591b-8bf6-1fa87f56a85e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-16428388-adc9-5bc3-a420-1ca62578bc67" :answer-field/choices ["answer-16428388-adc9-5bc3-a420-1ca62578bc67"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16428388-adc9-5bc3-a420-1ca62578bc67" :answer/id #uuid "16428388-adc9-5bc3-a420-1ca62578bc67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-72d27b98-5424-5f73-97fc-8f2eaa4b8548" :question/id #uuid "72d27b98-5424-5f73-97fc-8f2eaa4b8548" :question/math-academy-id "q-251896" :question/problem "Consider the two sets of $7$ paired observations shown in the table below.\n\n| **$\\,{x}_{i}\\,$** | $12$ | $14$ | $9$ | $17$ | $15$ | $10$ | $14$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$\\,{y}_{i}\\,$** | $15$ | $18$ | $11$ | $10$ | $20$ | $15$ | $16$ |\n\nGiven that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2}=1\\,231,$ calculate ${S}_{xx}.$" :question/worked-solution "Given a set of $n$ paired observations ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ and ${y}_{1},{y}_{2},…,{y}_{n},$ the sum of squared deviations from the mean for the data ${x}_{i}$ can be calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}^{2}-\\frac{1}{n}{({\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the sum of the ${x}_{i}$ data:\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}=12+\\,14+\\,9+\\,17+\\,15+\\,10+\\,14=91.\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}{x}_{i}^{2}=1\\,231.$\n\nFinally, by substituting into the above formula, we get\n\n$$\n{S}_{xx}=1\\,231-\\frac{1}{7}(91)^{2}=1231-1\\,183=48.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-273080ef-8c7f-5a88-9950-91456455d22a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-273080ef-8c7f-5a88-9950-91456455d22a" :answer-field/id #uuid "273080ef-8c7f-5a88-9950-91456455d22a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-24b92e1b-6dac-56bd-afde-abf287b17941" :answer-field/choices ["answer-debcb05c-cb0f-5de9-87ca-767431d038bf" "answer-55462a77-e788-50b5-b111-e635b1fd0381" "answer-1e2c88d9-7183-503f-8f87-d5f2453b6ce6" "answer-24b92e1b-6dac-56bd-afde-abf287b17941" "answer-d64241a1-b9bd-5245-9d38-1c834a4c5c12"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-debcb05c-cb0f-5de9-87ca-767431d038bf" :answer/id #uuid "debcb05c-cb0f-5de9-87ca-767431d038bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{S}_{xx}=119" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55462a77-e7