 #uuid "4ea44857-e35f-51f3-a0fe-716b02fb3232" :question/math-academy-id "q-108103" :question/problem "If $\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=10$ and $\\operatorname{ln}⁡y=2$, then $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the product rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n{log}_{n}⁡a+{log}_{n}⁡b={log}_{n}⁡(ab)\n$$\n\nUsing the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y \\\\  & =10+2 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-36b051f5-bf1c-54e5-8a93-26e5b24b1e4e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-36b051f5-bf1c-54e5-8a93-26e5b24b1e4e" :answer-field/id #uuid "36b051f5-bf1c-54e5-8a93-26e5b24b1e4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5cc6b6a6-43be-5279-9c28-d4a15b97a7cd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-87cbfab1-bb2d-5b42-b1df-3089693d6029" "answer-5cc6b6a6-43be-5279-9c28-d4a15b97a7cd" "answer-8c5e26d6-7fb1-52eb-bd97-ef78fa48ede9" "answer-b1e3d3db-20d4-51c4-9b30-1d9e01636929" "answer-9840868f-b940-5ed2-9e5b-49430536cb5a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87cbfab1-bb2d-5b42-b1df-3089693d6029" :answer/id #uuid "87cbfab1-bb2d-5b42-b1df-3089693d6029" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10x+2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5cc6b6a6-43be-5279-9c28-d4a15b97a7cd" :answer/id #uuid "5cc6b6a6-43be-5279-9c28-d4a15b97a7cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c5e26d6-7fb1-52eb-bd97-ef78fa48ede9" :answer/id #uuid "8c5e26d6-7fb1-52eb-bd97-ef78fa48ede9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1e3d3db-20d4-51c4-9b30-1d9e01636929" :answer/id #uuid "b1e3d3db-20d4-51c4-9b30-1d9e01636929" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20xy" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9840868f-b940-5ed2-9e5b-49430536cb5a" :answer/id #uuid "9840868f-b940-5ed2-9e5b-49430536cb5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{10}{y}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186111877 :tutorial/content "We can simplify the addition of two logarithms that share a base using the **product rule** for logarithms.\n\nThe **product rule** states that two logarithms which share a common base $\\color{blue}n$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\log_{\\color{blue}n}(a) + \\log_{\\color{blue}n}(b) = \\log_{\\color{blue}n}\\left( ab\\right).\n$$\n\nSo, we can use the product rule to rewrite $\\log_{\\color{blue}5}(4) + \\log_{\\color{blue}5}(3)$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡4+{log}_{5}⁡(3) & ={log}_{5}⁡(4\\cdot 3) \\\\  & ={log}_{5}⁡(12).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe product rule works exactly the same for the natural and common logarithms." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186110842 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id 17592186495042 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cae6f157-aca0-5d45-812b-7c9eb68fbca5" "question-1ced6944-9e50-5164-8d33-69e2545adde3"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cae6f157-aca0-5d45-812b-7c9eb68fbca5" :question/id #uuid "cae6f157-aca0-5d45-812b-7c9eb68fbca5" :question/math-academy-id "q-68910" :question/problem "In a store, there are three different types of cream cheese that come in boxes: \n\n- Box $A$ contains $1$ cup and costs $$1.96\\,.$\n\n- Box $B$ contains $1.2$ cups and costs $$2.40\\,.$\n\n- Box $C$ contains $1.5$ cups and costs $$2.94\\,.$\n\nWhich box of cream cheese is the best deal?" :question/worked-solution "The best deal is the one with the lowest unit price. So, we need to compute the unit prices for all three boxes. To compute the unit price, we divide the price by the total number of cups.   \n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of cups in box $A,$ we get\n\n$$\n1.96÷1=1.96\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $A$ is $$1.96.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of cups in box $B,$ we get\n\n$$\n2.40÷1.2=2\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $B$ is $$2.00.$\n\n- Dividing the total cost by the number of cups in box $C,$ we get\n\n$$\n2.94÷1.5=1.96\\,.\n$$\n\nSo, the unit price of box $C$ is $$1.96$  too.\n\nFrom the above, we see that boxes $A$ and $C$  have the lowest unit price. Therefore, boxes $A$ and  $C$ are the best deal." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3a5096d0-40bb-5c75-b8cd-0eaec3bf79bb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3a5096d0-40bb-5c75-b8cd-0eaec3bf79bb" :answer-field/id #uuid "3a5096d0-40bb-5c75-b8cd-0eaec3bf79bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-05de32c3-68cd-56f4-805b-b87c3fa65534" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c54814ec-8175-53f6-8edc-9fc045e757b3" "answer-093acaf7-e084-5171-b05c-2abfb2565913" "answer-05de32c3-68cd-56f4-805b-b87c3fa65534" "answer-b2001ae7-2e08-52d6-89a9-f372a3e6c52d" "answer-2530f346-332f-5442-ab0f-89084d832824"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c54814ec-8175-53f6-8edc-9fc045e757b3" :answer/id #uuid "c54814ec-8175-53f6-8edc-9fc045e757b3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-093acaf7-e084-5171-b05c-2abfb2565913" :answer/id #uuid "093acaf7-e084-5171-b05c-2abfb2565913" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05de32c3-68cd-56f4-805b-b87c3fa65534" :answer/id #uuid "05de32c3-68cd-56f4-805b-b87c3fa65534" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2001ae7-2e08-52d6-89a9-f372a3e6c52d" :answer/id #uuid "b2001ae7-2e08-52d6-89a9-f372a3e6c52d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2530f346-332f-5442-ab0f-89084d832824" :answer/id #uuid "2530f346-332f-5442-ab0f-89084d832824" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186495043 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d5b928b2-4413-5ea5-b176-1122913e3fcf" "question-344d25f1-e189-5dcd-8b33-971f6adcaf13" "question-33438ac4-91a4-539b-acda-ce62d65ce1c2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d5b928b2-4413-5ea5-b176-1122913e3fcf" :question/id #uuid "d5b928b2-4413-5ea5-b176-1122913e3fcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-68936" :question/problem "Nathan, a freelance journalist, charges $$0.04$ per word for his financial articles. How many words would it take for him to earn $1$ dollar?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the unit rate of $$0.04$ per word (dollars per word). To find how many words  it would take for him to earn $1$ dollar we need to find the unit rate in words per dollar. So, we take the reciprocal: \n\n$$\n0.04\\,\\text{dollars per word}\\,\\to \\,1÷0.04=25\\,\\text{words per dollar}\n$$\n\nSo, the unit rate is $25$ words per dollar. Therefore, Nathan writes $25$ words for $1$ dollar." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c63c13a8-c976-5993-9a85-24d526e9a808"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c63c13a8-c976-5993-9a85-24d526e9a808" :answer-field/id #uuid "c63c13a8-c976-5993-9a85-24d526e9a808" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8633dbcf-f937-517b-8467-a84b85c9b404" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4006bf8e-d408-5915-8dae-5778affcbf40" "answer-6f64e556-b780-5f32-80a5-22ca75df18a0" "answer-8633dbcf-f937-517b-8467-a84b85c9b404" "answer-493744f2-c626-56a3-8d5a-5b93b57f4207" "answer-0889992d-3157-57fa-a016-613a47a3e111"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4006bf8e-d408-5915-8dae-5778affcbf40" :answer/id #uuid "4006bf8e-d408-5915-8dae-5778affcbf40" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$16$ words" :db/ensure [